WEBVTT

00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:08.800
Maria Watches Over Us

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:16.140
Spreading a blank map wide open
Shiroi chizu ookiku hiroge

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:23.120
Let's go hide the treasure box
Takara-bako kakushi ni ikou

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:31.190
No need for coats or even hats
Kooto nante iranai boushi mo ne

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:38.860
Armed with just mechanical pencil lead
Shaapen no shin dake haite

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:42.200
Round and round and round,
Kururu kururu ku

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:46.170
Running through
kakenukeru

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:49.110
Round and round and round,
Kururu kururu ku

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:54.070
Our footprints mark the X
ashiato wa batsu-jirushi da yo

00:00:54.520 --> 00:01:01.050
Passing through the walls of the school
Kousha no kabe tsuki-nuke

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:09.360
We can go anywhere, there will be a path there
Dokonimo ikeru soko ni michi ga aru

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:16.560
The pleats of our skirts won't be disturbed
Sukaato no hida midare-nai

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:23.870
If it's a secret journey
Himitsu no tabi nara

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:35.960
While we were at the amusement
park during exam break,

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:38.720
my dear sister became ill and collapsed.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:41.490
Love
Crocheting

00:01:45.130 --> 00:01:50.090
I rode home with my dear sister and
Kashiwagi-san, who had come with us.

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:54.140
But even now, several days later,

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:58.100
Kashiwagi-san's words still linger in my ears.

00:01:59.050 --> 00:02:02.150
Defeating me won't give you victory.

00:02:02.150 --> 00:02:02.880
What?

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:07.550
Meaning, if you're jealous of me,
you've still got a long way to go.

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:09.960
Don't settle for what you've got now,

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:12.320
and aspire to attain something on a higher level.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:24.310
The fact that he's telling me such things...

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:27.500
...already puts me so far behind
Kashiwagi-san that I'll never catch up.

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:30.340
Even though I want to be of
greater help to Sachiko-sama...

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:39.750
Who was that?

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:56.040
An Unexpected Guest

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:04.440
Mother, you didn't call for me...

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:06.710
...did you?

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:11.150
Is something wrong?

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:14.720
I felt like someone called my name just now...

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:24.860
Yes? Fukuzawa residence.

00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:29.860
Oh, thank you for all you did the other day.

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:32.700
One moment please.

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:37.380
It's Kashiwagi-san.

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:39.710
Hello?

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:43.180
Oh, Yumi-chan, sorry for
calling you out of the blue.

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:45.050
Has something happened?

00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:49.710
Uh... Yes. It's actually about Toko.

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:50.980
Toko-chan?

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:53.560
I guess she's not over there
by the sound of that.

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:55.360
What about Toko-chan?

00:03:55.930 --> 00:03:59.420
It's late and she's not home yet,
so the Matsudairas are worried.

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:00.400
What?

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:05.210
The truth is, earlier in the day,
the family sort of had a fight.

00:04:05.210 --> 00:04:07.110
A slight difference of opinion, if you will,

00:04:07.110 --> 00:04:08.840
and it seems she ran out of the house.

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:12.510
So, I'm looking into all of the likely places...

00:04:12.610 --> 00:04:14.550
Have you checked with
Sachiko-sama's residence?

00:04:15.050 --> 00:04:17.480
I'm calling from the Ogasawara estate.

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:21.220
The Matsudairas said they don't
want to make a big fuss about this,

00:04:21.220 --> 00:04:23.210
so I came here as if I were just dropping by.

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:26.460
Have you told Sachiko-sama about this?

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:28.730
I was planning on letting her know,

00:04:28.730 --> 00:04:31.200
but it seems Hasekura-san
is visiting with her, so...

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:32.530
Rei-sama?

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:34.230
I'll try some other places.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:35.560
Thank you.

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:38.600
Has something happened?

00:04:40.610 --> 00:04:42.980
One of my underclassmen,
someone who Kashiwagi-san also knows well,

00:04:42.980 --> 00:04:44.470
is apparently late coming home.

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:47.570
I see. That's worrisome.

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:48.780
Yeah...

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:52.210
Kashiwagi-san is such a nice young man.

00:04:52.920 --> 00:04:56.580
If only someone like him would
take you for his bride.

00:04:57.690 --> 00:04:59.250
Stop that.

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:02.400
Wait, that's not how you should be reacting.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:03.460
This is where you should go,

00:05:03.460 --> 00:05:07.460
"Oh, Mother! What are you saying?! Quit it!"

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:08.630
Right?!

00:05:16.140 --> 00:05:18.610
So, to what do I owe this visit today?

00:05:18.610 --> 00:05:20.810
Aren't you here because you want to talk to me?

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:27.750
Yoshino's become friendly
with an underclassman.

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:29.190
I see.

00:05:31.590 --> 00:05:33.530
She's a third-year in middle school.

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:36.220
It's a girl named Nana Arima.

00:05:36.860 --> 00:05:38.560
Have you been introduced to her?

00:05:39.030 --> 00:05:40.190
No.

00:05:40.970 --> 00:05:44.230
It's more like I happened to see them
in the midst of all the confusion.

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:45.390
Confusion?

00:05:45.810 --> 00:05:49.500
Oh, I went to a match-making meeting.
That's when I saw them.

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:51.140
A match-making meeting?!

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:55.200
Oh, but I only learned later that
it was a match-making meeting.

00:05:55.280 --> 00:05:57.440
I just met with the son of a family friend.

00:05:57.950 --> 00:06:00.290
I heard he was having the
same surgery as Yoshino,

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:02.020
so I wanted to be encouraging.

00:06:03.660 --> 00:06:05.650
How old is he?

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:08.260
10 years old.

00:06:09.660 --> 00:06:11.660
I thought it might be something like that.

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:19.070
That's when Yoshino appeared
unannounced with a girl named Nana.

00:06:20.710 --> 00:06:23.840
I don't care how they met or when...

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:28.650
But why hasn't Yoshino said anything to me?

00:06:29.720 --> 00:06:30.480
Rei.

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:32.280
I know.

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:34.850
I'm going to be graduating...

00:06:35.320 --> 00:06:38.420
...and Yoshino should find
someone to be her little sister.

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:42.590
I just...

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:50.060
Stop.

00:06:54.310 --> 00:06:55.210
Sorry.

00:06:56.110 --> 00:06:58.440
Why are you so anxious?

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:08.180
I'm thinking of not going to
Lillian Women's College.

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:11.350
I thought you submitted an application.

00:07:11.630 --> 00:07:12.960
I'll have it withdrawn.

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:15.050
Does Yoshino-chan know about this?

00:07:15.260 --> 00:07:16.160
I haven't told her.

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:16.990
Why not?

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:18.760
I'm scared.

00:07:19.070 --> 00:07:23.300
I feel like if she asks me why,
my resolve might waver...

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:27.640
And your decision is, in part,
for Yoshino-chan's sake, isn't it?

00:07:29.410 --> 00:07:31.900
I've lived all my life watching Yoshino.

00:07:32.710 --> 00:07:36.270
But she doesn't need my protection anymore.

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:40.560
I thought I'd spend the
rest of my life by her side,

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:42.390
but I've been left behind.

00:07:44.490 --> 00:07:49.900
Still, if I can't let go of her
before she leaves the nest,

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:51.130
it will be pitiful.

00:07:57.910 --> 00:08:00.170
Thank you for listening.

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:10.320
Is it all right for us to be riding in tandem?

00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:12.840
This is in our yard, so it should be fine.

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:13.990
Right.

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:18.390
I'm impressed with your resolve.

00:08:18.490 --> 00:08:21.490
I have renewed respect for you.

00:08:22.630 --> 00:08:23.890
Me, too.

00:08:41.880 --> 00:08:43.080
Well, then...

00:08:43.550 --> 00:08:44.310
Rei.

00:08:45.220 --> 00:08:46.020
What is it?

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:50.520
I'm going to Lillian Women's College.

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:52.960
I see.

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:55.860
I'm going to remain at Lillian, where Yumi is.

00:08:57.500 --> 00:08:58.590
I understand.

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:02.860
What is the matter?

00:09:03.840 --> 00:09:06.270
Somehow, I just...

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:10.170
...found that moving.

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:16.840
Places where Toko-chan might go...

00:09:18.220 --> 00:09:19.210
I'm back.

00:09:22.220 --> 00:09:24.250
Yumi-chan, come here for a second!

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:36.400
Toko-chan!

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:39.640
Good evening, Yumi-sama.

00:09:40.110 --> 00:09:42.270
I just happened to run into
her on the corner there.

00:09:42.440 --> 00:09:44.880
So I invited her to drop by.

00:09:49.050 --> 00:09:51.080
A-Anyway, come on in.

00:09:52.490 --> 00:09:54.590
Pardon me for the late visit.

00:09:54.590 --> 00:09:55.760
It's fine!

00:09:55.760 --> 00:09:58.120
I know! We're having dinner soon,
so you should join us.

00:09:58.460 --> 00:10:01.160
Oh, no, I will be leaving shortly.

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:02.860
Don't be shy.

00:10:02.860 --> 00:10:05.590
Wait in Yumi's room until we're ready to eat.

00:10:05.970 --> 00:10:07.130
Yes, ma'am.

00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:12.800
Here you are.

00:10:13.110 --> 00:10:15.610
Do Yoshino-sama and Shimako-sama
come here often as well?

00:10:15.610 --> 00:10:19.810
No, no one from school has
visited since I started high school.

00:10:19.810 --> 00:10:21.150
You're the first.

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:22.440
What?

00:10:23.080 --> 00:10:24.640
What about Sachiko Onee-sama?

00:10:24.820 --> 00:10:27.620
She's come to the front of the house,

00:10:27.620 --> 00:10:29.820
but she's never been inside.

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:31.050
Oh, no.

00:10:31.330 --> 00:10:32.880
Then I cannot.

00:10:33.460 --> 00:10:35.090
Hold on a second, Toko-chan.

00:10:36.300 --> 00:10:38.000
To allow me into your room...

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:41.830
...before your dear sister
or your close friends is...

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:44.670
It's not about the order with these things, right?

00:10:44.670 --> 00:10:46.670
Or are you worried about
going into my room...

00:10:46.670 --> 00:10:50.040
...when no one else has
tested the waters before you?

00:10:52.780 --> 00:10:53.550
No.

00:10:53.550 --> 00:10:54.950
Then it's fine, right?

00:10:54.950 --> 00:10:55.940
Come on, now.

00:10:58.990 --> 00:11:00.590
Just find a comfortable seat.

00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:01.680
All right.

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:03.520
What a wonderful room.

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:11.920
So, you've already called Noriko-san?

00:11:12.830 --> 00:11:15.430
I haven't called anyone yet.

00:11:16.100 --> 00:11:18.770
Did Suguru Onii-sama call you?

00:11:18.770 --> 00:11:20.610
Or was it Sachiko-sama?

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:22.010
It was Kashiwagi-san.

00:11:22.010 --> 00:11:26.950
Sachiko-sama has a guest over,
so it seems he hasn't told her yet.

00:11:34.590 --> 00:11:36.180
Wasn't it cold out there?

00:11:36.660 --> 00:11:39.180
No, because I was walking.

00:11:39.830 --> 00:11:40.920
The whole time?

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:43.960
The whole time.

00:11:44.570 --> 00:11:47.400
So you walked all the way over here...

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:48.900
Yes.

00:11:53.640 --> 00:11:56.110
Did you come to see me?

00:12:02.550 --> 00:12:05.050
I was walking deep in thought...

00:12:05.050 --> 00:12:07.610
...and before I knew it, I had come a long way.

00:12:10.730 --> 00:12:13.160
I looked at the lot number
written on the utility pole...

00:12:13.160 --> 00:12:15.560
...and it was close to your address,

00:12:15.560 --> 00:12:17.090
so I wondered where your place might be.

00:12:18.900 --> 00:12:21.170
But it was growing darker by the minute,

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:23.570
so I was about to give up and head home...

00:12:23.570 --> 00:12:25.270
...when I ran into Yuki-san.

00:12:25.510 --> 00:12:26.600
I see.

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:30.840
But the upshot of it is that she came here.

00:12:32.810 --> 00:12:34.280
Poor thing.

00:12:34.280 --> 00:12:36.940
Toko-chan's hands were really cold.

00:12:40.590 --> 00:12:44.990
Right now, I want to warm her
chilled body without saying a word.

00:12:45.530 --> 00:12:48.390
I want to let her tired soul rest.

00:12:53.300 --> 00:12:55.360
Yumi! Dinner!

00:13:04.650 --> 00:13:06.370
Then, shall we go?

00:13:10.620 --> 00:13:12.180
Thank you for the meal.

00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:14.320
I will be leaving soon.

00:13:14.490 --> 00:13:16.650
What? Leaving? Where?

00:13:17.060 --> 00:13:18.290
Home.

00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:21.500
Thanks to you, I've been
able to cool my head nicely...

00:13:21.500 --> 00:13:23.160
...and if I don't return home,

00:13:23.160 --> 00:13:26.300
my parents will wear years
off their lives with worry.

00:13:26.300 --> 00:13:27.700
I-I see.

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:29.360
I'll see you home.

00:13:29.540 --> 00:13:31.870
Oh, no, I will call a taxi.

00:13:32.440 --> 00:13:35.430
Oh, if it's a ride, I've already called for one.

00:13:35.910 --> 00:13:36.600
What?

00:13:42.350 --> 00:13:43.580
Thank you for everything.

00:13:44.020 --> 00:13:45.950
I will come again to thank you properly.

00:13:48.390 --> 00:13:49.690
Thank you for the meal.

00:13:50.390 --> 00:13:52.120
Come visit us again.

00:13:55.760 --> 00:13:57.860
Toko-chan's such a nice girl.

00:13:58.470 --> 00:14:01.920
If only a girl like her would
become your little sister.

00:14:02.140 --> 00:14:05.730
Mother! What are you saying?! Quit it!

00:14:06.640 --> 00:14:10.740
Your reaction is clearly different
from when I mentioned Kashiwagi-san.

00:14:13.880 --> 00:14:16.910
Yumi-chan, I think you might
be a bad poker player.

00:14:18.390 --> 00:14:21.220
The day after Toko-chan's unexpected visit,

00:14:21.220 --> 00:14:23.380
Kashiwagi-san came to thank us.

00:14:24.590 --> 00:14:27.460
Toko-chan's mother had taken to
her bed due to shock,

00:14:27.860 --> 00:14:31.530
so he said he had been asked
to represent the Matsudaira family.

00:14:43.080 --> 00:14:43.670
What is it?

00:14:44.450 --> 00:14:47.710
Do you know why Toko-chan
ran away from home?

00:14:48.420 --> 00:14:50.010
What if I do know?

00:14:50.320 --> 00:14:53.050
Would it be too much to ask for you to tell me?

00:14:53.050 --> 00:14:54.210
What did Toko have to say?

00:14:54.520 --> 00:14:56.390
I couldn't bring myself to ask her somehow.

00:14:56.920 --> 00:14:59.450
But in spite of that, you would still like to know?

00:14:59.860 --> 00:15:02.190
That will be up to how you feel.

00:15:03.060 --> 00:15:04.190
How I feel?

00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:07.500
It's not a matter that
I can disclose to just anyone.

00:15:08.200 --> 00:15:10.500
But if it's you,

00:15:10.500 --> 00:15:12.470
I'll tell you at my own discretion.

00:15:13.310 --> 00:15:17.710
Listen to me. It would mean
learning Toko's secret.

00:15:17.710 --> 00:15:20.870
And you'll be learning it behind Toko's back.

00:15:22.920 --> 00:15:25.650
The question is, do you have the
resolve to deal with that?

00:15:27.290 --> 00:15:28.650
I...

00:15:29.160 --> 00:15:33.130
For your own sake and for Toko's sake,

00:15:33.130 --> 00:15:35.430
think it over again before you ask me.

00:15:37.430 --> 00:15:40.990
But the next time you ask me, I'll answer.

00:15:45.270 --> 00:15:47.970
The resolve to deal with it...

00:15:53.850 --> 00:15:54.520
What?!

00:15:54.520 --> 00:15:56.680
Shh! Keep your voice down!

00:16:00.420 --> 00:16:01.760
But you just said...

00:16:01.760 --> 00:16:05.630
...that you're inviting Arima Nana-san
to today's Christmas party...

00:16:05.630 --> 00:16:08.490
And that's why I'm asking for your cooperation.

00:16:08.630 --> 00:16:09.990
Cooperation?

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:15.330
In other words, you're saying you want
to invite Toko-chan and Kanako-chan, too.

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:17.040
I'm not saying that.

00:16:17.040 --> 00:16:18.540
Now, now...

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:20.710
That way, I can get on the bandwagon...

00:16:20.710 --> 00:16:23.880
...and say, "In that case,
maybe I'll invite a friend, too."

00:16:23.880 --> 00:16:25.880
That's how I want to go about it.

00:16:25.880 --> 00:16:27.310
What's with that?

00:16:27.310 --> 00:16:28.340
No?

00:16:28.780 --> 00:16:33.080
Yoshino-san, did you promise Arima
Nana-san to become soeurs with her?

00:16:33.520 --> 00:16:34.720
Not yet.

00:16:34.720 --> 00:16:36.850
But you're still going to bring her?

00:16:37.420 --> 00:16:40.090
Nana's asking to be introduced to Rei-chan...

00:16:40.960 --> 00:16:42.360
Really...

00:16:42.760 --> 00:16:46.060
I haven't seen Toko-chan since that day.

00:16:46.700 --> 00:16:50.500
If her friend, Noriko-chan,
innocently asks her to come along,

00:16:50.500 --> 00:16:52.100
I might be able to see her naturally.

00:16:52.710 --> 00:16:54.330
All right, I understand.

00:16:54.680 --> 00:16:56.070
I'll help you!

00:16:59.410 --> 00:17:00.950
About today's party...

00:17:00.950 --> 00:17:02.320
There aren't that many of us,

00:17:02.320 --> 00:17:05.620
so I'm thinking I'd like to
invite a couple more people.

00:17:05.620 --> 00:17:08.960
Do either of you have anyone
you'd like to invite?

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:10.750
I don't really...

00:17:11.690 --> 00:17:13.430
Can you think of anyone, Noriko?

00:17:13.430 --> 00:17:14.550
Not especially.

00:17:14.860 --> 00:17:17.530
Then, what about Toko-chan and Kanako-chan?

00:17:17.530 --> 00:17:19.330
Oh, that's a good idea.

00:17:19.330 --> 00:17:22.170
Noriko-chan, would you try inviting those two?

00:17:22.640 --> 00:17:23.660
I do not want to.

00:17:25.370 --> 00:17:26.670
What did you just...

00:17:27.510 --> 00:17:28.910
I said that I do not want to.

00:17:29.310 --> 00:17:30.710
Hey, Noriko-chan!

00:17:30.710 --> 00:17:31.650
Why?

00:17:31.650 --> 00:17:34.140
Why don't you want to invite them to the party?

00:17:34.480 --> 00:17:37.250
I merely do not want to be
the one inviting them.

00:17:37.250 --> 00:17:39.890
You are the one who brought
their names up, Yumi-sama.

00:17:39.890 --> 00:17:43.380
Then would it not be logical that you
should be the one to invite them?

00:17:43.890 --> 00:17:46.950
At any rate, I decline to do this.

00:17:50.100 --> 00:17:51.330
I understand.

00:17:52.900 --> 00:17:55.870
In that case, I will go.

00:17:56.070 --> 00:17:56.730
What?

00:17:58.510 --> 00:18:00.970
There is no reason for you to go, Onee-sama!

00:18:00.970 --> 00:18:02.600
I wanted Yumi-sama to...

00:18:02.910 --> 00:18:06.750
If we absolutely must ask Yumi-san to do this,

00:18:06.750 --> 00:18:08.520
then tell us the reason for that.

00:18:08.520 --> 00:18:12.610
Wouldn't that also follow the logic
that you are so particular about?

00:18:15.120 --> 00:18:17.610
I'm sorry, Shimako-san! I'll go!

00:18:18.290 --> 00:18:20.850
Oh, then, shall we go together?

00:18:21.900 --> 00:18:25.700
Noriko-chan, I'm sorry for asking you
to do something so troublesome.

00:18:30.640 --> 00:18:33.870
Why did you think to go invite them yourself?

00:18:34.510 --> 00:18:39.050
I just had this nebulous thought
that Toko-chan ought to be invited.

00:18:39.050 --> 00:18:40.380
Nebulous?

00:18:41.520 --> 00:18:43.680
Because there tend to be...

00:18:43.680 --> 00:18:47.380
...surprisingly important things hiding
in those nebulous thoughts.

00:18:52.990 --> 00:18:53.760
I'm sorry.

00:18:56.630 --> 00:18:58.670
What are you saying sorry for?

00:18:58.670 --> 00:19:03.940
The reason things got like this
between you and Shimako-san...

00:19:03.940 --> 00:19:05.970
I feel like it might be my fault...

00:19:05.970 --> 00:19:07.410
So I'm sorry.

00:19:08.340 --> 00:19:09.580
Pardon me,

00:19:09.580 --> 00:19:13.050
but I still do not understand what
you are apologizing to me for.

00:19:13.050 --> 00:19:18.640
I'm the one who originally suggested inviting
Toko-chan and Kanako-chan to the party.

00:19:20.390 --> 00:19:25.150
Basically, I've decided to invite a
certain underclassman to the party.

00:19:25.630 --> 00:19:26.820
I see...

00:19:29.130 --> 00:19:30.060
Oh!

00:19:30.700 --> 00:19:35.030
Should I be saying
"congratulations" in this case?

00:19:35.240 --> 00:19:37.400
We're still far from getting to that stage.

00:19:38.070 --> 00:19:41.910
So you see, at any rate,
I'm the one to blame for this.

00:19:42.410 --> 00:19:45.210
Blame? Please...

00:19:45.450 --> 00:19:47.150
But hearing that...

00:19:47.150 --> 00:19:50.550
...has softened your resentment
towards Yumi-san a little, right?

00:19:51.920 --> 00:19:54.250
This is what you really wanted to say, right?

00:19:54.250 --> 00:19:58.460
"If you want to invite Toko,
you should invite her yourself, Yumi-sama."

00:19:58.460 --> 00:20:02.390
"Is that how little Toko means
to you, Yumi-sama?"

00:20:06.370 --> 00:20:10.390
I do know that this is a problem
between the two of them, but...

00:20:10.870 --> 00:20:13.740
Yeah, I know. You're friends.

00:20:13.740 --> 00:20:16.900
You worry about them, even when
they haven't asked you to, right?

00:20:18.250 --> 00:20:19.110
Yes.

00:20:22.920 --> 00:20:24.350
Today?

00:20:24.590 --> 00:20:25.550
Are you unavailable?

00:20:25.790 --> 00:20:28.520
I have something to do in the early evening, so...

00:20:28.790 --> 00:20:29.880
What about you, Toko-chan?

00:20:31.490 --> 00:20:33.050
I...

00:20:33.930 --> 00:20:35.390
I am also a bit...

00:20:36.260 --> 00:20:38.390
I see. Then...

00:20:38.700 --> 00:20:43.000
Oh, but if we could be
pardoned for leaving early,

00:20:43.000 --> 00:20:45.300
we would love to attend.

00:20:45.440 --> 00:20:46.910
Right, Toko-san?

00:20:46.910 --> 00:20:47.640
What?

00:20:48.040 --> 00:20:50.310
At the Rose Mansion after Mass, correct?

00:20:50.310 --> 00:20:51.210
Um...

00:20:53.110 --> 00:20:54.880
Is there anything we should bring?

00:20:55.350 --> 00:21:00.380
No, though we might want your help
before we get the party started.

00:21:00.850 --> 00:21:01.820
Of course.

00:21:02.090 --> 00:21:05.390
Please let us know if there
is anything we can do.

00:21:09.730 --> 00:21:11.130
Then we'll see you later.

00:21:11.270 --> 00:21:12.030
Yes.

00:21:23.740 --> 00:21:27.510
Toko-chan has good friends.

00:21:28.250 --> 00:21:29.880
I was thinking the same thing.

00:21:43.460 --> 00:21:45.950
"Thank you for the other day."

00:21:46.430 --> 00:21:48.400
In that one bow,
Toko-chan expressed the sentiments...

00:21:48.400 --> 00:21:50.700
...that she would not put into words.

00:21:51.840 --> 00:21:54.170
Toko-chan has a bit of a contrary streak.

00:21:54.270 --> 00:21:57.240
But she's also serious and extremely sensitive.

00:21:58.180 --> 00:22:01.840
That's why she probably always
guards her heart with many layers.

00:22:02.650 --> 00:22:05.910
So that she can withstand minor
attacks here and there.

00:22:09.720 --> 00:22:14.490
I'm arbitrarily imagining how Toko-chan
must be and thinking I understand her.

00:22:16.130 --> 00:22:18.150
But what should I do?

00:22:18.870 --> 00:22:23.000
At this rate, I feel like Toko-chan will
grow further and further apart from me.

00:22:23.870 --> 00:22:26.570
The question is, do you have
the resolve to deal with that?

00:22:29.010 --> 00:22:30.140
The resolve...

00:22:44.730 --> 00:22:47.790
A winterscape where even...
Machi no irodori sae doko

00:22:47.790 --> 00:22:52.360
...the town's colors seem forlorn somehow
to naku samishige na fuyu no keshiki

00:22:52.730 --> 00:22:56.540
I think of you, turning your back on me...
Senaka mise kaketeitta

00:22:56.540 --> 00:23:00.270
...and running off
anata o omou

00:23:01.240 --> 00:23:05.280
There's a clear square pane...
Futari no aida ni wa

00:23:05.280 --> 00:23:09.280
...between the two of us
toumei na shikakkei

00:23:09.280 --> 00:23:12.020
It's misted over right now...
Ima wa kasunderu

00:23:12.020 --> 00:23:18.620
...with the crystals of sighs
tame-iki no kesshou de

00:23:19.230 --> 00:23:23.300
Window glass, window glass
Mado garasu mado garasu

00:23:23.300 --> 00:23:29.240
It's clouded and I can't see you
Kumottete anata ga mienai no

00:23:29.240 --> 00:23:35.140
Even though I know that you're there
Soko ni iru koto wa wakatteiru no ni

00:23:35.280 --> 00:23:39.180
Are you smiling? Are you crying?
Waratteru naiteru no

00:23:39.180 --> 00:23:45.080
I don't even care if you're frowning, let me see you
Shikamettsura demo ii kara misete

00:23:45.190 --> 00:23:53.650
Wipe the glass from your side, too
Sochira no hou kara mo garasu o fuite

00:24:06.010 --> 00:24:07.010
Preview

00:24:07.010 --> 00:24:08.410
Preview
Oh, I feel so nervous.

00:24:08.410 --> 00:24:11.550
Preview
How should I introduce Nana to
everyone at the Christmas party?

00:24:11.550 --> 00:24:14.280
Preview
Is that such a difficult thing to do?

00:24:14.280 --> 00:24:16.120
Preview
It would be one thing if I
were the one feeling nervous.

00:24:16.120 --> 00:24:16.520
Preview
What?

00:24:16.520 --> 00:24:18.420
Preview
After all, for a middle school student,

00:24:18.420 --> 00:24:20.850
Preview
the Rose Mansion is a distant,
unapproachable place.

00:24:20.850 --> 00:24:23.390
Preview
Even as she says that, it's as
though Nana feels no pressure...

00:24:23.390 --> 00:24:25.930
Preview
...and I find that both envious and infuriating...

00:24:25.930 --> 00:24:26.560
Preview
Next time, "The Blank Map to the Future."

00:24:26.560 --> 00:24:27.830
Preview
Next time, "The Blank Map to the Future."
The Blank Map to the Future

00:24:27.830 --> 00:24:30.630
Preview
Because it's unknown,
the future is both scary and fun.
The Blank Map to the Future

00:24:30.630 --> 00:24:32.470
Preview
But I never imagined that such a terrible thing...
The Blank Map to the Future

00:24:32.470 --> 00:24:35.040
Preview
...would happen to Yumi-san
on the day of the party.
The Blank Map to the Future

00:24:35.040 --> 00:24:35.900
Preview
The Blank Map to the Future
